From 9bc83afe2ed53a71b600e49a0f678168315a8ceb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:38:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur: Describe the GPU zap shader

glymur.dtsi reserves gpu-microcode@919fe000 for the Adreno zap shader but
never hands it to the GPU node. Without a zap-shader child the a8xx driver
falls back to writing RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL itself:

  Zap shader not enabled - using SECVID_TRUST_CNTL instead

On the ASUS Zenbook A14 (UX3407NA) that leaves the machine running until
a heavier GPU workload (e.g. changing the GNOME wallpaper), at which point
the secure world resets the SoC with no kernel log and nothing in pstore.

Add the zap-shader node referencing the existing carveout, mirroring
hamoa.dtsi. Boards supply the signed firmware via firmware-name.

Signed-off-by: kelsey <11334159+kernelzeroday@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
index a71724698..64bf8a6b3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur.dtsi
@@ -4670,6 +4670,10 @@ gpu: gpu@3d00000 {
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
 			interconnect-names = "gfx-mem";
 
+			gpu_zap_shader: zap-shader {
+				memory-region = <&gpu_microcode_mem>;
+			};
+
 			gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 				compatible = "operating-points-v2-adreno",
 					     "operating-points-v2";
-- 
